<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450411" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 5 — Nested table (table inside a table cell)</title>
   <refbody>
      <section id="sec_d755e7">
         <p>Consider a table where the author has placed a second complete <codeph>&lt;table&gt;</codeph> element inside one of the <codeph>&lt;td&gt;</codeph> cells of an outer table.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Nested table inside table cell</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_xlw_vyn_lkc">
&lt;table>
  &lt;tr>
    &lt;td>Label&lt;/td>
    &lt;td>
      &lt;table>
        &lt;tr>
          &lt;td>Sub-item A&lt;/td>
          &lt;td>Value 1&lt;/td>
        &lt;/tr>
        &lt;tr>
          &lt;td>Sub-item B&lt;/td>
          &lt;td>Value 2&lt;/td>
        &lt;/tr>
      &lt;/table>
    &lt;/td>
  &lt;/tr>
&lt;/table></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_mng_wyn_lkc">
&lt;table frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1" id="table_outer">
  &lt;tgroup cols="2">
    &lt;colspec colnum="1" colname="col1"/>
    &lt;colspec colnum="2" colname="col2"/>
    &lt;tbody>
      &lt;row>
        &lt;entry>Label&lt;/entry>
        &lt;entry>
          &lt;table frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1" id="table_inner">
            &lt;tgroup cols="2">
              &lt;colspec colnum="1" colname="col1"/>
              &lt;colspec colnum="2" colname="col2"/>
              &lt;tbody>
                &lt;row>
                  &lt;entry>Sub-item A&lt;/entry>
                  &lt;entry>Value 1&lt;/entry>
                &lt;/row>
                &lt;row>
                  &lt;entry>Sub-item B&lt;/entry>
                  &lt;entry>Value 2&lt;/entry>
                &lt;/row>
              &lt;/tbody>
            &lt;/tgroup>
          &lt;/table>
        &lt;/entry>
      &lt;/row>
    &lt;/tbody>
  &lt;/tgroup>
&lt;/table></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p><b>Result:</b> The converter identifies the nested <codeph>&lt;table&gt;</codeph> element and preserves it as a CALS <codeph>&lt;table&gt;</codeph> inside the parent table cell. The inner table is wrapped in a <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element inside the outer <codeph>&lt;entry&gt;</codeph> to separate the nested structure from the parent cell content.</p>
         <note type="warning"> Nested tables increase complexity and may affect rendering, accessibility, and publishing output. Flatten the nested structure into a single table where possible.</note>
      </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
